==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|săt}}, {{IPA|en|/sæt/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Pvanp7-sat.wav|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-sat.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æt|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
See {{m|en|sit}}.

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|sit||ed-form}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''sat''' in the middle of the park.}}
#: {{ux|en|Jill '''sat''' Jack down for a talk.}}
#: {{ux|en|We '''sat''' ourselves down for dinner.}}
#: {{ux|en|The children were '''sat''' at a low table. {{q|informal; chiefly UK/Commonwealth}}}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In parts of the UK, the past participle ''sat'' may be colloquially used in place of ''sitting'' in sentences such as: ''this morning, I was '''sat''' at the bus stop waiting for the bus''.  See also {{m|en|stood}}.

=====Translations=====
{{checktrans-top}}
* Woiwurrung: {{t-check|wyi|ngorrn-i}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Etymology 2===
Clippings.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{abbreviation of|en|satisfactory}}.
# {{abbreviation of|en|satisfied}}.
# {{abbr of|en|saturated}}.

